cript/","lens":{"theater":[0,0,0,0.0],"cinema":[0,0,0,0.0],"imax":[0,0,0,0.0],"streaming":[0,0,0,0.0],"dtc":[0,0,0,0.0],"ai_spend":[0,0,0,0.0],"tariffs":[0,0,0,0.0],"pricing_power":[9,4,5,28.45],"cost_cuts":[0,0,0,0.0],"guidance":[0,0,0,0.0,{"raise":0,"reaffirm":0,"cut":0}],"ai_disruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":0.0986,"r5":0.1407,"r20":0.0092,"r1_spy":0.1006,"r5_spy":0.1417,"r20_spy":0.0216}}],"quotes":[{"c":"GFF 2018 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2018-11-14","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ronald Kramer","x":"Segment adjusted EBITDA grew by 40% to $177 million, driven by the increase in revenue, partially offset by the effects of higher input costs, including tariffs in commodities and the incorporation of the acquisitions initially operating at lower margins than our existing businesses, as expected.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/14/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2018 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2018-11-14","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Brian Harris","x":"Our guidance does not include the potential 15% increase in Section 301 tariffs expected in January 2019.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/14/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2018 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2018-11-14","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian Harris","x":"Our organic EBITDA seems of lag our price realization in offsetting increased input costs, integration innovation related investments for the ClosetMaid and CornellCookson acquisitions and Defense Electronics EBITDA consistent with 2018 EBITDA levels.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/14/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2018 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2018-11-14","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian Harris","x":"We would expect to pass these through additional costs if and when that become effective.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/14/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2018 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2018-11-14","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Andrew Casella","x":"I just wanted to see if there were any other cash inflows or outflows or any restructuring charges that we should be mindful of?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/14/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q1","e":"gff","d":"2019-01-31","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kramer","x":"Segment adjusted EBITDA increased 31% to $52 million, driven by higher revenue and the related drivers of its growth, partially offset by increased input costs and tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/31/griffon-corp-gff-q1-2019-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q1","e":"gff","d":"2019-01-31","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kramer","x":"So we've dealt with whatever tariff impact is out there, we'll continue to deal with it.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/31/griffon-corp-gff-q1-2019-earnings-conference-call.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q2","e":"gff","d":"2019-05-02","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ronald Kramer","x":"Segment-adjusted EBITDA increased 23% to $49 million driven primarily by revenue, partially offset by increased input cost, including raw materials and the effects of tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/03/griffon-corporation-gff-q2-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q2","e":"gff","d":"2019-05-02","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ronald Kramer","x":"The other thing that I would add is if you remember going into this year, we have talked about $70+ million of potential negative impact from tariffs and other things and I'm happy to say that we've worked our way through all of it and that's no longer a concern of our outlook.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/03/griffon-corporation-gff-q2-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2019-08-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ronald Kramer","x":"Segment adjusted EBITDA increased 16% to $57.8 million driven primarily by increased revenue and partially offset by increased material and tariff costs for Ames and CBP.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/02/griffon-corporation-gff-q3-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2019-08-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ronald Kramer","x":"We also are continuing to work with our customers and suppliers to mitigate the effects of price inflation including due to tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/02/griffon-corporation-gff-q3-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2019-08-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian Harris","x":"For the materials and the tariffs, we had significant headwinds initially and we had set price or put our price increases to offset those amounts.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/02/griffon-corporation-gff-q3-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2019-08-01","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian Harris","x":"We are working with our customers already and actually started that process when we passed through increases related to the 10% tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/02/griffon-corporation-gff-q3-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2019-08-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald Kramer","x":"But over time the ability to innovate, the ability to take cost out of the combined business gives us a real platform of growth and we expect our margins and free cash flow to continue to reflect that.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/02/griffon-corporation-gff-q3-2019-earnings-call-tran.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2019-11-13","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kramer","x":"We react to things that are moving the landscape of issues that have been out there over the last year are still unsettled, most importantly trade and tariffs are still there.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/14/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2019-11-13","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"Look at the impact, the trade, and tariff, how much it hurt us this year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/14/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2019-11-13","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"So this is more about our own operating efficiency than it is about the price pass-through.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/14/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2019-11-13","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Justin Bergner","x":"If we look back on 2019, you obviously got a pretty big benefit from price and mix, and there is an element of price that was more or less passing through tariffs or inflation immediately or in a lag.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/14/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2019 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2019-11-13","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"This is about the management teams being able to adapt in a new environment of increased costs to be able to take cost out of the business, and the pricing is with a lag.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/14/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2020 Q2","e":"gff","d":"2020-04-28","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"Adjusted EBITDA was $25 million decreasing 13% due to reduced sales and tariffs, partially offset by contribution from Apta.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/28/griffon-corp-gff-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"GFF 2020 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2020-07-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"Adjusted EBITDA was $37 million, increasing 55% from the prior year quarter due to the increased revenue as mentioned a moment ago, partially offset by increased tariffs and COVID-19 related costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/30/griffon-corp-gff-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2020 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2020-07-30","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"Like many other companies, last quarter, we withdrew our guidance because of the uncertainties arising out of the COVID-19 pandemic.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/30/griffon-corp-gff-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2020 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2020-11-12","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Trey Grooms","x":"I'll pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/12/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2020 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2020-11-12","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kramer","x":"We also announced today that Telephonics implemented an initiative to improve its operational efficiencies through streamlining its organization and consolidating facilities.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/12/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2020 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2020-11-12","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"The one-time charges are comprised of $46 million of cash charges, which includes $26 million of personnel-related costs such as training, severance and duplicate personnel costs, as well as $20 million of facility and lease exit costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/12/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2020 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2020-11-12","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"Regarding Q1 in 2021 -- regarding guidance, like many other companies we withdrew our guidance in our fiscal second quarter because of uncertainties arising out of the COVID-19 pandemic.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/12/griffon-corp-gff-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q1","e":"gff","d":"2021-01-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kramer","x":"And the margin improvement story is going to be one that is going to evolve based on both volume mix and there will always be issues like the price of steel that will be a pass through item for us and for most of corporate America.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/28/griffon-corp-gff-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q1","e":"gff","d":"2021-01-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kramer","x":"…a positive for recovering economy and the ability to mitigate those input costs, continue to pass along price increases as a result is what the balance of this year is going to look like and we continue to believe that we can do that successfully, maintain and/or improve our margins by doing it.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/28/griffon-corp-gff-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q1","e":"gff","d":"2021-01-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kramer","x":"Telephonics is taking actions to improve its operational efficiencies by streamlining its organization and consolidating facilities, which Brian will also discuss in a little more detail.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/28/griffon-corp-gff-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q1","e":"gff","d":"2021-01-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"During the first quarter, AMES incurred pre-tax restructuring-related exit cost of approximately $3 million supporting the AMES strategic initiative.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/28/griffon-corp-gff-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q2","e":"gff","d":"2021-04-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"Well, in general and for the third quarter as we continue to work and the timing of the price increase, the lag of price increases come into play Q3 could see some pressure, and we'll see the offset of that once we get into Q4 and beyond.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/griffon-corp-gff-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q2","e":"gff","d":"2021-04-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"It's similar, so we're still working the price increases into the third quarter and there'll be a lag so we'll expect to have that done in full benefit of it in the fourth quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/griffon-corp-gff-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q2","e":"gff","d":"2021-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"Excluding restructuring-related charges, gross profit was $174 million increasing 13.2% over the prior year quarter with gross margin increasing 30 basis points to 27.4%.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/griffon-corp-gff-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q2","e":"gff","d":"2021-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"Excluding restructuring-related charges from both periods selling, general and administrative expenses were $123 million or 19.3% of revenue compared to $122 million or 21.5% in the prior year quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/griffon-corp-gff-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q2","e":"gff","d":"2021-04-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Ronald J. Kramer","x":"So -- but with clearly a confidence level that we chose to take this moment to increase our guidance for the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/griffon-corp-gff-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q2","e":"gff","d":"2021-04-29","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Bob Labick","x":"Did I hear you correctly, you're actually raising guidance?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/griffon-corp-gff-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2021-07-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Ron Kramer","x":"We're continuing to pass along price increases and we're continuing to try to mitigate the inflationary trends that are going on for us and across all the economy and our view as the consumer is strong.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/griffon-corporation-gff-q3-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2021-07-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Ron Kramer","x":"So we see this is evolutionary for our business and we're going to continue to find ways to pass along price increases and take cost out of our business in order to improve our margins.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/griffon-corporation-gff-q3-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2021-07-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brian Harris","x":"Excluding restructuring-related charges, gross profit was $171 million increasing 3.5% compared to the prior-year quarter with gross margin increasing 30 basis points to 26.4%.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/griffon-corporation-gff-q3-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2021-07-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brian Harris","x":"Excluding restructuring-related charges, selling, general and administrative expenses were $122 million or 18.9% of revenue compared to $112 million or 17.7% in the prior-year quarter, primarily driven by restoration of selling and marketing expenditures and increased distribution and…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/griffon-corporation-gff-q3-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2021-07-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Ron Kramer","x":"Our businesses are proven to be resilient and we are reiterating our full-year guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/30/griffon-corporation-gff-q3-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2021-11-16","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"Just to dimension [Phonetic] the magnitude of the price increases we have realized and expect to realize, we secured multiple double-digit price increases in '21 and expect to realize additional double-digit price increases in the first half of fiscal '22.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/16/griffon-corporation-gff-q4-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2021-11-16","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"…starting in the latter part of our second quarter and will reach more normalized levels by our fourth quarter, reflecting the pass-through of pricing to our customers and expected improvement in labor and transportation availability, along with improving reliability within our supply chain.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/16/griffon-corporation-gff-q4-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2021-11-16","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"Excluding restructuring-related charges, gross profit was $159 million, increasing 3% compared to the prior-year quarter, with gross margin decreasing 10 basis points to 27.9%.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/16/griffon-corporation-gff-q4-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"GFF 2021 Q4","e":"gff","d":"2021-11-16","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brian G. Harris","x":"Excluding restructuring-related charges, selling, general and administrative expenses were $120 million or 21% of revenue compared to $116 million or 21% in the prior-year quarter, with the increased dollars primarily driven by distribution, transportation and incentive costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/16/griffon-corporation-gff-q4-2021-earnings-call-tran/"},{"c":"GFF 2026 Q2","e":"gff","d":"2026-05-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian Harris","x":"I will point out that Clopay had price increases recently issued, mid-single digit that were effective at the end of March.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/griffon-gff-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2026 Q2","e":"gff","d":"2026-05-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian Harris","x":"So we have another price increase that has started.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/griffon-gff-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2026 Q2","e":"gff","d":"2026-05-07","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Unknown Analyst","x":"As we think about your fiscal second half, you reiterated the full year guide, but any changes to the underlying assumptions around the end markets?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/07/griffon-gff-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2026 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2026-08-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian Harris","x":"And looking forward, we had a price increase during the quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/12/griffon-gff-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"GFF 2026 Q3","e":"gff","d":"2026-08-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Brian Harris","x":"We had the price increase, as I just mentioned, that was to offset increa